    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d770-a7">

                <pb facs="0878" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg798"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Arthur, United States consular agent at Oaxaca, to
                        Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consular Agency</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Oaxaca</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-09-07"><hi rendition="#italic">September 7,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have made a careful investigation in
                    regard to the Americans reported to be confined in jail in this city “<hi
                        rendition="#italic">on account of railroad accidents growing out of the
                        movement of trains in the Republic of Mexico.</hi>”</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">I find absolutely none</hi>. About three years ago an
                    engineer had charge of a train and became so intoxicated that the conductor, who
                    was in about the same condition, undertook to run the engine and wrecked the
                    train and killed one man. Both conductor and engineer were confined for about
                    six months.</p>
                <p>Since this accident no arrests have been made, but to my personal knowledge
                    several brakemen have been killed by moving trains.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Chas. H. Arthur</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consular Agent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
